1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,610
Arby’s.

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,090
R. B.

3
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:04,500
Roast beef.

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,840
That sounds like a mystery solved.

5
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,720
Except those letters
stand for something else.

6
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:13,410
And once you learn the stories
behind these four restaurant names,

7
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:17,020
you might never read their
signs quite the same way again.

8
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:21,090
Picture a roast-beef sandwich
beside two enormous letters.

9
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:22,490
R and B.

10
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,020
Say them together.

11
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,200
“Arby.”

12
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:30,428
But according to Arby’s parent company,
the name refers to the Raffel Brothers:

13
00:00:30,468 --> 00:00:31,990
Leroy and Forrest.

14
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,860
They founded the restaurant
in Boardman, Ohio, in 1964.

15
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,620
Raffel Brothers.

16
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:40,250
R. B.

17
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,610
Arby’s.

18
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,200
The initials belong to the founders.

19
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:48,660
The roast beef makes the coincidence
especially easy to believe.

20
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:51,600
That’s what makes this
a good naming mystery.

21
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:54,960
The answer seems to be sitting
right there on the menu.

22
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:58,980
But the real explanation is
standing behind the counter.

23
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:04,286
Two brothers whose initials became a
name millions of customers would say when

24
00:01:04,326 --> 00:01:05,630
ordering lunch.

25
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,650
Now let’s move from two
brothers to one daughter.

26
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,600
Who was Wendy?

27
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:15,530
If your answer is “the founder’s
daughter,” you’re on the right track.

28
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:17,540
But there’s another detail.

29
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:19,540
Her name was Melinda.

30
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:24,254
Dave Thomas considered his children’s
names before choosing Melinda’s nickname

31
00:01:24,294 --> 00:01:25,770
for the restaurant.

32
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:31,955
Wendy’s official history explains that her
siblings had trouble pronouncing her name.

33
00:01:31,995 --> 00:01:34,470
“Wenda” eventually became “Wendy.”

34
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,660
A family nickname became
a restaurant name.

35
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:40,060
Imagine that transformation.

36
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:43,770
At home, it’s a name your
brothers and sisters call you.

37
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:47,140
Outside, it becomes a
sign above a restaurant.

38
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:51,134
Then customers start saying it
without knowing anything about the

39
00:01:51,174 --> 00:01:52,510
family behind it.

40
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:56,150
The name sounds like a person
because it came from one.

41
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:00,230
But the story sits one layer
beneath the obvious answer.

42
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,960
Wendy was real.

43
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:04,360
Wendy was also a nickname.

44
00:02:04,610 --> 00:02:08,170
Now for a name with something
you can actually picture.

45
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:13,230
You hear “Taco Bell,” and the words
seem perfectly matched to the logo.

46
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,170
A taco restaurant.

47
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:16,440
A bell.

48
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:19,740
But the Bell is also a person.

49
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:25,400
Glen Bell founded the chain, opening
its first restaurant in Downey,

50
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,070
California, in 1962.

51
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,710
His surname is right there in the brand.

52
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,800
Once you know that, the
name reads differently.

53
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:36,880
It isn’t simply a food
followed by a familiar object.

54
00:02:37,130 --> 00:02:39,510
It’s the food followed by the founder.

55
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:43,050
The bell symbol makes the
name easy to visualize.

56
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:46,200
But the family name
gives it another meaning.

57
00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:49,300
We’ve now found brothers,
a daughter’s nickname,

58
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,760
and a founder hiding in plain sight.

59
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:54,790
Our last stop takes us
somewhere quite different.

60
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:57,950
A coffee shop name that leads to a novel.

61
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,110
Before we reveal this one, take a guess.

62
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,770
Was Starbucks named after a founder?

63
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,480
A type of coffee?

64
00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:07,440
Or a character in a book?

65
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:10,480
The book holds the answer.

66
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:15,815
According to Starbucks, the name was
inspired by Starbuck—the first mate aboard

67
00:03:15,855 --> 00:03:18,810
the Pequod in Herman Melville’s Moby-Dick.

68
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:23,910
The name we associate with coffee has
a literary and seafaring connection.

69
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,800
Picture it on screen.

70
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:27,410
A book opening.

71
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:28,840
“Starbuck.”

72
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,290
Then the familiar coffee-shop name.

73
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:35,860
A surprising route to something we
now read without a second thought.

74
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:38,140
Four familiar names.

75
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:39,660
Two brothers.

76
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:41,460
A family nickname.

77
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:43,270
A founder’s surname.

78
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,890
And a sailor from a classic novel.

79
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:49,210
You don’t need to know any of
those stories to order lunch.

80
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:51,960
But knowing them changes what you notice.

81
00:03:52,210 --> 00:03:56,690
Next time you pass one of those signs,
you’ll see more than a restaurant name.

82
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,370
You’ll see a little piece of how it began.

83
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:01,740
Which story surprised you most?

84
00:04:01,990 --> 00:04:05,150
And what company name
should we investigate next?

85
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,010
Now you know.

86
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,110
Ordinary has secrets.
